vsm2.20:3.3:
Herein, the understanding that occurs by observing the specific characteristics of such and such
states thus, “Materiality (rūpa) has the characteristic of being molested (ruppana);
feeling has the characteristic of being felt,” is called full-understanding as the known.

vsm2.20:4.6:
for from there onwards the seven contemplations that effect the abandoning of the perception of permanence, etc., predominate thus:
(1) Contemplating formations as impermanent, a man abandons the perception of permanence. (2) Contemplating them as painful,
he abandons the perception of pleasure. (3) Contemplating them as not-self, he abandons the perception of self.
